Package: spdw-purge
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.8), python3-tk
Recommends: pkexec | policykit-1, deborphan
Suggests: flatpak
Homepage: https://github.com/sirpips/spdw-purge
Maintainer: sirpips <sirpips@users.noreply.github.com>
Description: cyberpunk disk analyzer and cleaner for Debian / MX Linux
 SPDW Purge finds what eats your disk and removes it. It combines a
 treemap/tree/file-type scanner, system and user junk cleaning (apt, journal,
 old kernels, logs, snapshots, caches), complete package removal with leftover
 hunting, and a finder for duplicates, empty files, broken links and big old
 files. Every action is confirmed, logged and can be rehearsed with DRY-RUN.
 .
 Made by sirpips - SPDW Factory Lab.
